  "title": "Dama and Dumang",
  "description": "Ramai Singh and a friend briefly play a tune of Mage Porob, a festival of the Ho people, with Singh on the dama and his friend on the dumang. In Ho, they explain to Lalit Singh Banra how these drums are made. Subhashish Panigrahi recorded them at Keshpada, Mayurbhanj district, Odisha, India, for his 2019 documentary Mage Porob. The footage wasn't used in the film, and it was edited and published under the 𑢼𑣃𑣃𑣊 𑢾𑣁𑣌𑣁𑣖 (Ruum Sakam) project in 2024. Ho subtitles and the Odia and English translations are by Ganesh Birua, edited by Panigrahi.",
